\ Spitfire: points and directions in the ground frame, as arrays of three:
\ metres east (x), up (y) and north (z). An attitude is a frame of three unit
\ directions at right angles, :right, :up and :forward, the axes of whatever
\ it belongs to, the aircraft or the eye.

\ arithmetic on points and directions
: v+ ( a b -- a+b ) ' + 2 nmap ;
: v- ( a b -- a-b ) ' - 2 nmap ;
: v* ( a k -- a*k )
	| a k |
	a ( k * ) map ;
: v-dot ( a b -- product )
	| a b |
	a first b first * a second b second * + a 2 @i b 2 @i * + ;
: v-cross ( a b -- a×b )
	| a b |
	a spread to az to ay to ax
	b spread to bz to by to bx
	[ ay bz * az by * -  az bx * ax bz * -  ax by * ay bx * - ] ;
: v-length ( a -- length ) dup v-dot sqrt ;
: v-unit ( a -- a' )
	| a |
	a a v-length 1e-9 max2 1 swap / v* ;

\ the point a fraction of the way from one point to another
: v-between ( a b t -- point )
	| a b t |
	a b a v- t v* v+ ;

\ a direction turned by an angle about a unit axis (Rodrigues' formula)
: v-rotate ( v axis angle -- v' )
	| v axis angle |
	angle cos to c
	angle sin to s
	v c v*  axis v v-cross s v* v+  axis axis v v-dot 1 c - * v* v+ ;

\ a level attitude facing a compass heading in degrees, 0 north and 90 east
: heading-attitude ( degrees -- attitude )
	| degrees |
	degrees PI 180 / * to bearing
	[ bearing sin 0 bearing cos ] to forward
	{ :forward forward :up [ 0 1 0 ] :right [ 0 1 0 ] forward v-cross } ;

\ an attitude turned about one of its own axes; the other two axes turn with it
: turn-attitude ( attitude axis-key angle -- attitude' )
	| attitude axis-key angle |
	attitude axis-key @ to axis
	{ :right attitude@right axis angle v-rotate
	  :up attitude@up axis angle v-rotate
	  :forward attitude@forward axis angle v-rotate } ;

\ an attitude made square again after many small turns: forward kept, up made perpendicular to it, right from the two
: square-attitude ( attitude -- attitude' )
	| attitude |
	attitude@forward v-unit to forward
	attitude@up forward attitude@up forward v-dot v* v- v-unit to up
	{ :forward forward :up up :right up forward v-cross } ;

\ a direction in an attitude's own terms (right, up, forward) as a ground direction
: attitude>ground ( attitude local -- direction )
	| attitude local |
	local spread to ahead to rising to across
	attitude@right across v*  attitude@up rising v* v+  attitude@forward ahead v* v+ ;

\ a ground direction in an attitude's own terms
: ground>attitude ( attitude direction -- local )
	| attitude direction |
	[ attitude@right direction v-dot attitude@up direction v-dot attitude@forward direction v-dot ] ;

\ the compass heading of a direction in degrees, 0 north and 90 east
: heading-of ( direction -- degrees )
	| direction |
	direction first direction 2 @i atan2 180 PI / * 360 + 360 mod ;
